I think that invoking should be left to quest artifacts.  Also, if you
were using this weapon, you wouldn't have lycanthropy.  If you could
get it via sacrificing, you probably could have prayed as well.  So,
the lycanthropy cure seems almost redundant.

> > Ogresmasher: kills ogres instantly
> 
> Maybe increase strength of the player a fair amount when wielded, as
> well as the extra damage to ogres?

I think that's a great idea.  It would make the artifact a little more
generally useful.
 
> > Demonbane: does 2X damage against riders, as well (or more??)
> 
> How about simply preventing any demon hit from it from teleporting? 
> Also could absorb curses and stop some summoning.

Kind of like a cancelling effect? I think curse absorption is too
powerful.  From a programming standpoint I'm not sure how that would
work.  Perhaps demons cannot self-teleport when you wield demonbane?

Alternatively, maybe a chance (20%?) to stun demons (which would also
prevent teleport).
 
> > Tsurugi: always insta-kill engulfers
> 
> I'd allow it to absorb curses too, and increase the bisection chance. 
> This thing really has fallen into disrepair as-is.

Absorbing curses seems a little high, but a larger bisection chance
(in general) up to somewhere in the 7-10 range might make it more
useful too.

> > > Orcrist: 3X damage to orcs instead
> 
> Maybe also act as a light source when Orcs are around?

That's a good point.  Of course, from a literary sense Sting glows
when orcs are around too, but from a game standpoint gives warning. 
How would you differentiate the two artifacts?
 
> For what it's worth, I think Sunsword should become brighter in the
> presence of undead, stop undead from summoning other undead, and
> possibly can be invoked in order to turn?

Like I said before, I think invoking should be left to quest
artifacts.  I like the idea of it being brighter when there are undead
around (just as an effect, more than being useful).  Stopping undead
summoning is a little too powerful and would be the ultimate lich
weapon.  Perhaps having a chance to blind enemies or blind or confuse
undead when you are within its light radius?

